TIGunTemplate.description.140mmTungstenAutocannon_ETC=A 140mm autocannon that fires tungsten rounds using electromagnetic technology to achieve higher muzzle velocities and improved armor penetration.
TIGunTemplate.displayName.280mmAutocannon_LIPC=280mm Flux Powered LIPC Autocannon
TIGunTemplate.description.280mmAutocannon_LIPC=A LIPC (Laser‑Induced Plasma Channel) autocannon that utilizes flux energy to fire high-velocity projectiles with exceptional armor penetration capabilities.
TIGunTemplate.displayName.RailDriver_Small=Rail Driver (Small)
TIGunTemplate.displayName.RailDriver_Medium=Rail Driver (Medium)
TIGunTemplate.displayName.RailDriver_Large=Rail Driver (Large)
TIGunTemplate.displayName.RotaryKineticDriver_Small=Rotary Kinetic Driver - Light
TIGunTemplate.displayName.RotaryKineticDriver_Medium=Rotary Kinetic Driver - Standard
TIGunTemplate.displayName.RotaryKineticDriver_Large=Rotary Kinetic Driver - Heavy
TIGunTemplate.description.RailDriver_Small=A compact railgun that accelerates dense kinetic penetrators to hypervelocity using electromagnetic induction, ideal for close-range ship-to-ship combat.
TIGunTemplate.description.RailDriver_Medium=A medium-calibre railgun platform offering increased muzzle velocity and magazine capacity for sustained fire in fleet engagements.
TIGunTemplate.description.RailDriver_Large=A heavy railgun battery capable of delivering devastating kinetic strikes at extended range, favoured by capital ships as a primary anti-armour weapon.
TIGunTemplate.description.RotaryKineticDriver_Small=A rotary-barrel kinetic driver that maintains a high cyclic rate of fire by cycling multiple barrels, saturating point-defence systems with a stream of projectiles.
TIGunTemplate.description.RotaryKineticDriver_Medium=A medium rotary kinetic driver with improved projectile mass and rate of fire, effective against lightly armoured ships and incoming missiles alike.
TIGunTemplate.description.RotaryKineticDriver_Large=A large-calibre rotary kinetic driver providing withering fire volume against both warships and incoming ordnance at medium engagement ranges.
